<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>入住退房 on 编程那些事儿</title><link>https://before80.github.io/prgms/tags/%E5%85%A5%E4%BD%8F%E9%80%80%E6%88%BF/</link><description>Recent content in 入住退房 on 编程那些事儿</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>zh-cn</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:31:03 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://before80.github.io/prgms/tags/%E5%85%A5%E4%BD%8F%E9%80%80%E6%88%BF/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>酒店入住与退房：办入住、换房、问设施、延迟退房、核对账单</title><link>https://before80.github.io/prgms/Language/English/Learn/dialogue/occasions/hotel-checkin/</link><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://before80.github.io/prgms/Language/English/Learn/dialogue/occasions/hotel-checkin/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;在美国住酒店，前台的开场白几乎是固定的三句：&lt;code&gt;Do you have a reservation?&lt;/code&gt; → &lt;code&gt;ID and a credit card, please.&lt;/code&gt; → &lt;code&gt;You're all set.&lt;/code&gt;。听懂这三句，入住这一步就不会卡住。真正需要提前搞明白的，是&lt;strong&gt;卡上被冻住的那笔钱&lt;/strong&gt;。&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>